# Data Architecture
Data Architecture - design of systems to support the evolving data needs of an enterprise, achieved by flexible and 
reversible decisions reached through a careful evaluation of trade-offs

## Enterprise - design of systems to support change in an enterprise
-- Business - product or service strategy and business model
-- Application - structure and interaction of key applications
-- Technical - interaction of software and hardware components
-- Data - supporting the evolving data needs

Reversible decisions are key, i.e.:
-- One-way door decisions - irreversible decisions
-- Two-way door decisions - reversible decisions (eg storing data in s3 and changing the tier 
                            according to the business needs and frequency of the data usage)

## Conway's Law
Any organization that designs a system will produce a design whose structure is a copy of the
organization's communication structure - You need to understand the communication structure that
matches the company's communication channel

